From 5eab460162bb6746f3664f04e93730a7314a2266 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Code (independent review)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:22:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] Revise M4 proposal (R2.1): panel rule without half-width
 underflow or sum overflow

Address the two findings of the independent R2 review:
- F4: the panel rule multiplies by the width d (never 0 for a < b) with exact
  half weights; h only positions the nodes. Allowance term R_w MIN_VALUE / 2
  (tighter than R2's 8 K MIN_VALUE); node-position term includes underflow.
- F5: speeds as (mu, nu) pairs, ratios to the largest component, and a fixed
  product order chosen on d * S; G is never NaN and overflows only when the
  exact rule value does.

Adds M4R21RegressionTest (4 tests); the 54 existing M4 tests are unchanged.
Reference data unchanged. No production code; M1, M2 and M3 untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017wk67VdfTJWcfKRwchBikr
